      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Clarendon Plantation was founded before 1760 a few miles north of Town Creek on the Cape Fear River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.carolana.com/NC/Towns/Clarendon_NC.html",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1825 the plantation operated a water‑powered rice machine, one of the earliest in the Lower Cape Fear region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.carolana.com/NC/Towns/Clarendon_NC.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The village that grew around Clarendon never received a U.S. post office and soon vanished from maps.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.carolana.com/NC/Towns/Clarendon_NC.html",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1834 Clarendon Plantation boasted a brick barn with an attached mill house and two threshing mills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.carolana.com/NC/Towns/Clarendon_NC.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "A 1834 description called Clarendon a comfortable dwelling house, typical of Cape Fear plantation homes.",
